==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|skemtiligr||amusing, interesting, pleasant|lang=non}}, confer the Old Norse {{term|óskemtiligr||dull, uninteresting|lang=non}}, {{term|skemtiliga||amusingly, pleasantly|lang=non}}, {{term|skemta||to amuse, to entertain|lang=non}}, {{term|skemtan||an entertainment|lang=non}} or {{term|skemtun||an entertainment|lang=non}} and {{term|skemtanligr||amusing, pleasant|lang=non}}.

===Adjective===
{{is-adj-01|skemmtileg|skemmtilegt|skemmtilegri|skemmtilegastur}}

# [[funny]], [[amusing]]{{jump|is|funny|s}}
#: ''Systir hans þykir '''skemmtileg'''.''
#:: His sister is considered to be '''amusing'''.
# [[entertaining]], [[diverting]]{{jump|is|entertaining|s}}
# [[interesting]]{{jump|is|interesting|s}}

